From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:22:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(training): the day's Effort counts the muscular load of
 the gym sessions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Today ring still read 18/100 after an hour of heavy lifting: the day's
Effort is heart-rate only and the previous fix only reached the workout.
Each analysed session's extra load, TRIMP(Claude's effort) − TRIMP(its
heart-rate effort), is summed per day and added to the day's own TRIMP, then
mapped back onto the 0-100 axis (the axis is logarithmic, so efforts are not
added directly), as WHOOP's Strength Trainer adds muscular load to Day Strain.
Applied in WhoopRepository's three merged daily readers (one line each), so
the ring, its tiles, Trends and the coach read the same number; nothing is
written back. The per-day extras follow TrainingStore.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
